 "tab-J-1": {
  "page": 21,
  "headers": [
   [
    "We show some examples in our demo page.",
    ""
   ],
   [
    "",
    ""
   ],
   [
    "",
    "MaskGCT supports zero-shot voice conversion by fine-tuning the S2A with a"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "a target speaker using a reference speech from the target speaker, without"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "acoustic tokens Aref extracted from the reference speech to predict the target"
   ]
  ],
  "rows": [
   [
    "",
    "Since Ssrc may retain some timbre information, we perform timbral"
   ],
   [
    "features input to the semantic codec encoder.",
    ""
   ],
   [
    "",
    "input mel-spectrogram features of the W2v-BERT 2.0 model, following the"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "FreeVC [74]. We fine-tune our S2A model using this training strategy. We show"
   ],
   [
    "",
    ""
   ],
   [
    "Hard Cases Evaluation",
    ""
   ],
   [
    "",
    "We evaluate the performance of MaskGCT on some hard cases (SeedTTS"
   ],
   [
    "to instances where large-scale TTS models,",
    ""
   ],
   [
    "",
    "hallucinations. These cases include phrases with repeating words, tongue twisters,"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "linguistic structures. Examples of such cases include: “the great greek grape"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "greek grapes”, “How many cookies could a good cook cook If a good cook"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "good cook could cook as much cookies as a good cook who could cook"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "thought. But the thought I thought wasn’t the thought I thought I thought. If the"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "thought had been the thought I thought, I wouldn’t have thought so much”."
   ]
  ]
 }
